{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525369-help-in-making-a-stylized-pack-of-werewolf-foes","id":1525369,"title":"Help in making a (stylized) pack of Werewolf foes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-12T03:22:15-08:00","id":1525369,"title":"Help in making a (stylized) pack of Werewolf foes","content":"Hello Werewolf fans!<br /> <br /> I'm running a Vampire Dark Ages 20th Anniversary campaign, and the characters are due to meet a Werewolf pack guarding a ruined tower they are going to reclaim as their own Domain (we are running a modified version of the Transylvania Chronicles).<br /> <br /> I imagined them as a Shadow Lord-led pack (the chief being an ancestor to Margrave Konietzko), trying to purify the Tihuta pass from Kupala's influence.<br /> <br /> They should be a challenge, an almost lethal one, but ultimately approachable, with a combination of cunning maneuvers and strategic confrontation.<br /> <br /> Can I ask you some creative input to give shape to an interesting group of foes? I'm not very familiar with Legacy Werewolf rules, though I have access to WtA 20 core, so even a simplified set of numbers and Powers would be enough.<br /> <br /> My current coterie Is made of<br /> <br /> A Tzimisce Knight with Horrid Form<br /> A Tzimisce Knight / sorceror with Thaumaturgy 5 (Movement of the Mund)<br /> A Salubri Warrior (Valeren 4)<br /> A Nosferatu Spy (Obfuscate 4)<br /> A Malkavian Oracle (Dementation 4)<br /> A Setite infernalist hunter (Serpentis 4)<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> they also have some other minor Disciplines, and should reach the Wolves in some time, they Will probably get access at least to a couple other level 3 Disciplines.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce Knight has some shady deals with Kupala, so they could possibily enlist help by some Banes.<br /> <br /> Thank you in advance !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-12T09:45:35-08:00","id":1525373,"title":"","content":"There isn't really an &quot;almost lethal&quot; with Garou. They are <i>amazingly</i> lethal. They live in a different genre of horror apart from vampires where everyone gets torn and shredded up at a moment's notice; not only would you properly have to worry about them, but anything involving the appearance of an entire pack would also entail having whatever enemy they're actually after showing up (they still don't just go after vampires, even if they are Shadow Lords), which is likely to be something like a group of fomori that can also do terrible, terrible things to the coterie, as combat-worthy possessed can also somewhat easily get to Strength 9 and have natural weapons and extra soak, while those of a less combat-primary bent will have an array of distractions and mind tricks like supernatural seduction or direct psychic attacks that can leave the unwary with trickles of pulped brain leaking out their nose. Powerful banes are also somewhat likely to be able to just flat out wipe you and the pack out by accident (nexus crawlers are like unreality tornadoes that can leave everyone around without their faces and standing on a floor of lava, silver, or silver lava, with their bones cracked or replaced by swamp debris).<br /> <br /> If you're playing this as a more casual kind of contact, the Lords are more likely to just use Raven's Curse/Under the Gun on you (-2 to the difficulty to hit the target with missile weapons like arrows, making a potential staking more likely; the curse can also persist for some time, possibly even permanently) and let the chips fall where they may until you become more persistent in bothering them. But the moment that happens, you're going to find out just why Horrid Form is no real match for Crinos. Or even combat fomori, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-12T10:11:08-08:00","id":1525375,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I know that Werewolves are the most awesome forms of horror Life out there in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> That said, I Need to take inspiration from them t\u00f2 present a foe that isn't trivial, but also isn't instakill\ud83d\ude03<br /> <br /> I suppose a small pack of ... Dunno, 3 newly-created Wolves who are not all combat monkeys could be used?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-12T10:54:29-08:00","id":1525378,"title":"","content":"You have werewolves statted in the Vampire books for this purpose, to be a challenge for the PCs but not the furry blenders of WtA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-12T10:57:04-08:00","id":1525379,"title":"","content":"Are you trying to create antagonists that are supposed to be used as someone who is a threat but not necessarily a conflict or are you looking for a boss fight?<br /> <br /> Because the three young Garou seems least fun you can get out of this setup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-12T11:39:03-08:00","id":1525381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525369-help-in-making-a-stylized-pack-of-werewolf-foes?p=1525378#post1525378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have werewolves statted in the Vampire books for this purpose, to be a challenge for the PCs but not the furry blenders of WtA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I could use them and add some Thaumaturgical paths or rituals to customise them, but I'd like some uniqueness and unpredictability. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 11-12-2023, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-12T11:40:52-08:00","id":1525382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525369-help-in-making-a-stylized-pack-of-werewolf-foes?p=1525379#post1525379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you trying to create antagonists that are supposed to be used as someone who is a threat but not necessarily a conflict or are you looking for a boss fight?<br /> <br /> Because the three young Garou seems least fun you can get out of this setup.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reclaiming the Pass would probably see the characters engage Kinfolk and Spirits first, and perhaps meet the Wolves singularly to get a first impression of the threat, but meeting the pack and taking the Tower would be Boss Fight territory, I'd say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-12T12:59:38-08:00","id":1525385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525369-help-in-making-a-stylized-pack-of-werewolf-foes?p=1525375#post1525375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I know that Werewolves are the most awesome forms of horror Life out there in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> That said, I Need to take inspiration from them t\u00f2 present a foe that isn't trivial, but also isn't instakill\ud83d\ude03<br /> <br /> I suppose a small pack of ... Dunno, 3 newly-created Wolves who are not all combat monkeys could be used?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't making any value judgements. Honestly, I'm perplexed about why you're setting up a game of personal horror and then expecting to just drop in the protagonists of a splatter horror game like it's nothing. If you do it, someone's going to get splattered; it's in the name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-13T13:58:15-08:00","id":1525409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525369-help-in-making-a-stylized-pack-of-werewolf-foes?p=1525382#post1525382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reclaiming the Pass would probably see the characters engage Kinfolk and Spirits first, and perhaps meet the Wolves singularly to get a first impression of the threat, but meeting the pack and taking the Tower would be Boss Fight territory, I'd say.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel a primer on social dynamics of the Garou would help here.<br /> <br /> Garou packs are usually centered around a Caern. The Caern is an especially blessed area where the gauntlet is thin and where the location is guarded by a powerful Spirit that resonates with the location. This place naturally draws many spirits to it as a congregating place, and some of these are drafted as defenders of the locale in the umbra and the real world.<br /> <br /> The local Garou gather around the Caern as their holy place and organise their resources in the broader location of the Caern - this construct is called the Sept and is both a logistical and political core that the Garou revolve around. The Sept considers all Garou that gravitate to the Caern as members and often contains multiple groups of kinfolk families - be it local wolves or humans.<br /> <br /> A small Caern will have a single pack tending to it and a handful of kinfolk around it. The larger the Caern, the larger the Sept. In the Dark Ages most Septs are of a single Tribe. The Garou most competant/politically active to Hold Sept positions take care of the spirits, laws, stories, rituals and other day to day operations. Occasionally a Sept may even appoint a kinfolk to a position like this.<br /> <br /> Now kinfolk are not combatants, even those that would be considered warriors among humans are incredibly weak and vulnerable to the things the Garou fight. They will keep them safe and while they may help with day to day work, scouting,information gathering, trading, crafts, rites,hunting and protection, they will not be taken to battle or sent to places Garou packs will. It is too dangerous for them and the Garou are law bound to protect them. This will become more flexible in the modern day, but as it stands the kinfolk are too valuable to waste on the tasks of the Garou.<br /> <br /> Spirits are also not servants of the Garou, they are partners who expect payment or service for the work they do.<br /> <br /> The first and greatest task of any Sept is to keep their Caern safe. This is one of those things that no Garou will even discuss. Everything else in the litany is interpreted and discussed, buy this never is.<br /> <br /> Outside this task the common tasks of the Garou of the Sept is fighting the Wyrm, doing their end of the deal with the spirits and pursuing their own agendas if they are lucky to find time for that between the duties to their Caern, their Sept and their family.<br /> <br /> Now considering the context here, what is this tower, what does domain mean to you and how would it pertain to a Sept that they would deploy a pack there?<br /> <br /> Nb. If you meant dormant Caern by &quot;domain&quot;, you have chosen the thing Garou will do anything to protect and recover and it's not going to be a skirmish - it is going to be an all out war.<br /> <br /> I would strongly suggest you look into something less valuable or something that might provoke an uneasy alliance to resolve.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-14T00:28:29-08:00","id":1525425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525369-help-in-making-a-stylized-pack-of-werewolf-foes?p=1525409#post1525409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would strongly suggest you look into something less valuable or something that might provoke an uneasy alliance to resolve.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>First thing that came to mind is that the pack was send there to investigate rumors of something tainted that has settled inside that tower, possibly a good way off from the caern. Some demonish-avatar-of-Kupala thingy would fit the setup, maybe even just a powerful koldun.<br /> That would at least provide a chance that the pack and the wyrm thing could soften each other up before there is a direct confrontation between the coterie and the pack, and raise the possibility for a strange bedfellows alliance on either side.<br /> <br /> Because<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525369-help-in-making-a-stylized-pack-of-werewolf-foes?p=1525375#post1525375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I know that Werewolves are the most awesome forms of horror Life out there in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> That said, I Need to take inspiration from them t\u00f2 present a foe that isn't trivial, but also isn't instakill\ud83d\ude03<br /> <br /> I suppose a small pack of ... Dunno, 3 newly-created Wolves who are not all combat monkeys could be used?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> It's not about a dice pool measuring contest, I think most posters in this thread would agree that a direct confrontation between vampires and werewolves under WtA rules just wouldn't be much fun for the players. Even a non-combat oriented beginner level Garou has the potential to dust a Neonate in a single round, given some unlucky rolls - if you use WtA rules for them, they aren't VtM NPCs anymore but WtA PCs that happen to be under your control. And werewolf PCs are designed to shred through groups of monsters.<br /> <br /> Balancing them by using Disciplines is a lot easier - if you really want to use WtA rules for the flavor, my recommendation is to at least use VtM combat rules and Disciplines in melee for them. You can bring in the unknown / surprises with their Gifts, just.. take care with the ones geared towards combat.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525369-help-in-making-a-stylized-pack-of-werewolf-foes?p=1525409#post1525409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nb. If you meant dormant Caern by &quot;domain&quot;, you have chosen the thing Garou will do anything to protect and recover and it's not going to be a skirmish - it is going to be an all out war.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what was meant is that the PCs plan to establish a (vampire) Domain, and it doesn't relate to the Shadow Lords. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12590\" data-vbnamecard=\"12590\">Manfr</a> correct me if I'm wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 11-14-2023, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-14T17:28:56-08:00","id":1525437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525369-help-in-making-a-stylized-pack-of-werewolf-foes#post1525369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello Werewolf fans!<br /> <br /> I'm running a Vampire Dark Ages 20th Anniversary campaign, and the characters are due to meet a Werewolf pack guarding a ruined tower they are going to reclaim as their own Domain (we are running a modified version of the Transylvania Chronicles).<br /> <br /> I imagined them as a Shadow Lord-led pack (the chief being an ancestor to Margrave Konietzko), trying to purify the Tihuta pass from Kupala's influence.<br /> <br /> They should be a challenge, an almost lethal one, but ultimately approachable, with a combination of cunning maneuvers and strategic confrontation.<br /> <br /> Can I ask you some creative input to give shape to an interesting group of foes? I'm not very familiar with Legacy Werewolf rules, though I have access to WtA 20 core, so even a simplified set of numbers and Powers would be enough.<br /> <br /> My current coterie Is made of<br /> <br /> A Tzimisce Knight with Horrid Form<br /> A Tzimisce Knight / sorceror with Thaumaturgy 5 (Movement of the Mund)<br /> A Salubri Warrior (Valeren 4)<br /> A Nosferatu Spy (Obfuscate 4)<br /> A Malkavian Oracle (Dementation 4)<br /> A Setite infernalist hunter (Serpentis 4)<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> they also have some other minor Disciplines, and should reach the Wolves in some time, they Will probably get access at least to a couple other level 3 Disciplines.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce Knight has some shady deals with Kupala, so they could possibily enlist help by some Banes.<br /> <br /> Thank you in advance !</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I have made a couple of starting Packs with W20 rules that could wipe out most challengers. Problem is that the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1436799-w20-enhancing-the-pack-optimal-initial-char-gen-pack#post1436799\">Pack is too modern</a> the anachronism is bad, or uses the wrong Tribes (this is a <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1436799-w20-enhancing-the-pack-optimal-initial-char-gen-pack?p=1440826#post1440826\">Wendigo + Uktena pack</a>, how do you make them arrive in Transylvania???).<br /> <br /> Even if your guys are very optimized, the posted werewolves are just too good at fighting.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T04:27:27-08:00","id":1525449,"title":"","content":"Usually I tend to agree, the Garou are pain in the rear end when it comes to Vampires and your bloodsicker more often than not ends up a stain on the claws<br /> Buuut...<br /> This area and Clan and Tribe combination is a bit different<br /> Even Canon materilds use the term &quot;Shadow Lord&quot; and not the Lupine<br /> The fact is, in the past more than a ten thousand years, since the Eldest and his army of Fiends waged a bloody war and released Kupala (more or less) the conflict never resolved<br /> More than ten millenia and a deluge passed and the Tzimisce still there and the Shadow Lords licking their wounds<br /> And this is not just a Vampire point of view, the Werewolf supplements also highlight this, to the point manipulation (or secret alliances...) rasied their ugly heads. Vladimir Rustovitch is a good example of this; while he battled Teutonic knights in 1313, his jealous brood mates plotted against him and arranged a ambush on his castle by the Shadow Lords, who killed all his servitors and brides. When Vladimir returned his Frenzy was terrible. Stories of the massacre are told even today on the campfires of Shadow Lord moots and even Tzimisce shudder when they hear what he did to his brood mates.<br /> And like every good Tzimsice, he was very good keeping gurdges; Vladimir's main concern was his revenge against the hated Lupines. Aware of Past Lives, he hunted the descendants of those Shadow Lords that attacked his castle.<br /> It took a mistake killing <b>Evelyn Constantine </b>a wealthy media mogul Shadow Lord's father to force her abd her whole sept to in several very heavy and ancient favors to finally kill Rustovitch<br /> And he wasn't a &quot;real&quot; Elder, embraced in 876 CE<br /> So in this case it is not that of a stretch to say, they could survive, after all the Tzimisce hold their ground and even waged multi-front wars and the Shadow Lord basically were forced to co-exist with them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 11-15-2023, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T04:40:14-08:00","id":1525450,"title":"","content":"Foum hungry<br /> Forum ate post<br /> Me angry<br /> <br /> Usually I tend to agree, the Garou are pain in the rear end when it comes to Vampires and your bloodsicker more often than not ends up a stain on the claws<br /> Buuut...<br /> This area and Clan and Tribe combination is a bit different<br /> Even Canon materilds use the term &quot;Shadow Lord&quot; and not the Lupine<br /> The fact is, in the past more than a ten thousand years, since the Eldest and his army of Fiends waged a bloody war and released Kupala (more or less) the conflict never resolved<br /> More than ten millenia and a deluge passed and the Tzimisce still there and the Shadow Lords licking their wounds<br /> And this is not just a Vampire point of view, the Werewolf supplements also highlight this, to the point manipulation (or secret alliances...) rasied their ugly heads. Vladimir Rustovitch is a good example of this; while he battled Teutonic knights in 1313, his jealous brood mates plotted against him and arranged a ambush on his castle by the Shadow Lords, who killed all his servitors and brides. When Vladimir returned his Frenzy was terrible. Stories of the massacre are told even today on the campfires of Shadow Lord moots and even Tzimisce shudder when they hear what he did to his brood mates.<br /> And like every good Tzimsice, he was very good keeping gurdges; Vladimir's main concern was his revenge against the hated Lupines. Aware of Past Lives, he hunted the descendants of those Shadow Lords that attacked his castle.<br /> It took a mistake killing <b>Evelyn Constantine </b>a wealthy media mogul Shadow Lord's father to force her abd her whole sept to in several very heavy and ancient favors to finally kill Rustovitch<br /> And he wasn't a &quot;real&quot; Elder, embraced in 876 CE<br /> So in this case it is not that of a stretch to say, they could survive, after all the Tzimisce hold their ground and even waged multi-front wars and the Shadow Lord basically were forced to co-exist with them\u200b<br /> You said the Tzimisce Knight has some shady deals with Kupala, so they could possibily enlist help by some Banes, this could help but I must ask,why the sorceror is on the path of Thaumaturgy <br /> ?<br /> Just a curious question ,why not Koldunism to make the furrballs combust? ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T09:21:00-08:00","id":1525457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525369-help-in-making-a-stylized-pack-of-werewolf-foes?p=1525450#post1525450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Foum hungry<br /> Forum ate post<br /> Me angry<br /> <br /> Usually I tend to agree, the Garou are pain in the rear end when it comes to Vampires and your bloodsicker more often than not ends up a stain on the claws<br /> Buuut...<br /> This area and Clan and Tribe combination is a bit different<br /> Even Canon materilds use the term &quot;Shadow Lord&quot; and not the Lupine<br /> The fact is, in the past more than a ten thousand years, since the Eldest and his army of Fiends waged a bloody war and released Kupala (more or less) the conflict never resolved<br /> More than ten millenia and a deluge passed and the Tzimisce still there and the Shadow Lords licking their wounds<br /> And this is not just a Vampire point of view, the Werewolf supplements also highlight this, to the point manipulation (or secret alliances...) rasied their ugly heads. Vladimir Rustovitch is a good example of this; while he battled Teutonic knights in 1313, his jealous brood mates plotted against him and arranged a ambush on his castle by the Shadow Lords, who killed all his servitors and brides. When Vladimir returned his Frenzy was terrible. Stories of the massacre are told even today on the campfires of Shadow Lord moots and even Tzimisce shudder when they hear what he did to his brood mates.<br /> And like every good Tzimsice, he was very good keeping gurdges; Vladimir's main concern was his revenge against the hated Lupines. Aware of Past Lives, he hunted the descendants of those Shadow Lords that attacked his castle.<br /> It took a mistake killing <b>Evelyn Constantine </b>a wealthy media mogul Shadow Lord's father to force her abd her whole sept to in several very heavy and ancient favors to finally kill Rustovitch<br /> And he wasn't a &quot;real&quot; Elder, embraced in 876 CE<br /> So in this case it is not that of a stretch to say, they could survive, after all the Tzimisce hold their ground and even waged multi-front wars and the Shadow Lord basically were forced to co-exist with them\u200b<br /> You said the Tzimisce Knight has some shady deals with Kupala, so they could possibily enlist help by some Banes, this could help but I must ask,why the sorceror is on the path of Thaumaturgy<br /> ?<br /> Just a curious question ,why not Koldunism to make the furrballs combust? ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Rustovitch's continued existence and heat can be chalked up to the way that WoD books would often bend over backwards to fellate V:tM. As to why a Koldun doesn't just combust them, fire stopped being a worthwhile countermeasure against Garou back in Revised (earlier, if the pack patron was Hyperion/Katanka-Sonnak), and Master of Fire has only become more effective since. You might as well ask why Garou don't just summon spirits of fire or the sun to incinerate every vampire.<br /> <br /> Yes. Why don't they? It seems to work well for the Corax.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T12:16:26-08:00","id":1525468,"title":"","content":"At the end of the day, the issue we have with using garou as written in WtA in a Vampire chronicle is that it would not be fair for the players.<br /> <br /> To put this in the best terms I can; You wouldn't put 4-5 Vohzd against the players alongside three 5th generation Elders. You want things to be challenging, not frustrating like a garou npc rolling 11 dice of damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T13:22:09-08:00","id":1525475,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone and thanks for the responses!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525369-help-in-making-a-stylized-pack-of-werewolf-foes?p=1525409#post1525409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel a primer on social dynamics of the Garou would help here.<br /> <br /> Garou packs are usually centered around a Caern. The Caern is an especially blessed area where the gauntlet is thin and where the location is guarded by a powerful Spirit that resonates with the location. This place naturally draws many spirits to it as a congregating place, and some of these are drafted as defenders of the locale in the umbra and the real world.<br /> <br /> The local Garou gather around the Caern as their holy place and organise their resources in the broader location of the Caern - this construct is called the Sept and is both a logistical and political core that the Garou revolve around. The Sept considers all Garou that gravitate to the Caern as members and often contains multiple groups of kinfolk families - be it local wolves or humans.<br /> <br /> A small Caern will have a single pack tending to it and a handful of kinfolk around it. The larger the Caern, the larger the Sept. In the Dark Ages most Septs are of a single Tribe. The Garou most competant/politically active to Hold Sept positions take care of the spirits, laws, stories, rituals and other day to day operations. Occasionally a Sept may even appoint a kinfolk to a position like this.<br /> <br /> Now kinfolk are not combatants, even those that would be considered warriors among humans are incredibly weak and vulnerable to the things the Garou fight. They will keep them safe and while they may help with day to day work, scouting,information gathering, trading, crafts, rites,hunting and protection, they will not be taken to battle or sent to places Garou packs will. It is too dangerous for them and the Garou are law bound to protect them. This will become more flexible in the modern day, but as it stands the kinfolk are too valuable to waste on the tasks of the Garou.<br /> <br /> Spirits are also not servants of the Garou, they are partners who expect payment or service for the work they do.<br /> <br /> The first and greatest task of any Sept is to keep their Caern safe. This is one of those things that no Garou will even discuss. Everything else in the litany is interpreted and discussed, buy this never is.<br /> <br /> Outside this task the common tasks of the Garou of the Sept is fighting the Wyrm, doing their end of the deal with the spirits and pursuing their own agendas if they are lucky to find time for that between the duties to their Caern, their Sept and their family.<br /> <br /> Now considering the context here, what is this tower, what does domain mean to you and how would it pertain to a Sept that they would deploy a pack there?<br /> <br /> Nb. If you meant dormant Caern by &quot;domain&quot;, you have chosen the thing Garou will do anything to protect and recover and it's not going to be a skirmish - it is going to be an all out war.<br /> <br /> I would strongly suggest you look into something less valuable or something that might provoke an uneasy alliance to resolve.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> said, the Domain in question would be a vampiric one: the Coterie is reclaiming this deserted ruin, to create a Haven and a Library of important Noddist lore. The tower stands on this pass, and is a place of significance both because of an association with Kupala, and because it defended a critical juncture between Wallach principalities and the Ukrainian plains and steppes.<br /> <br /> As the Transylvania Chronicles mentions passingly that PCs may need to fight Werewolves in the area <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> and frankly the first part of the Chronicle is not that engaging, I wanted to work a bit around this plot, and envisioned that the Pass may be investigated by a small force of Werewolves, coming from the nearby Brooding Sky Sept.<br /> <br /> So, it's neither a Sept nor a dormant Caern, more a tainted place that local Shadow Lords wish to sanitize: they don't need to be an important expeditionary force, I would see them more as a small band seeking Renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T13:25:28-08:00","id":1525476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525369-help-in-making-a-stylized-pack-of-werewolf-foes?p=1525437#post1525437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I have made a couple of starting Packs with W20 rules that could wipe out most challengers. Problem is that the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1436799-w20-enhancing-the-pack-optimal-initial-char-gen-pack#post1436799\">Pack is too modern</a> the anachronism is bad, or uses the wrong Tribes (this is a <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1436799-w20-enhancing-the-pack-optimal-initial-char-gen-pack?p=1440826#post1440826\">Wendigo + Uktena pack</a>, how do you make them arrive in Transylvania???).<br /> <br /> Even if your guys are very optimized, the posted werewolves are just too good at fighting.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Really interesting thread! The Packs you worked on are way more optimized than I'd need, I'd like to present them with some interesting complementary challenges to their powers. If, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> said, it's not really feasible to use WtA, I suppose I will take a look at your sheets and do some reskin using Disciplines and Thaumaturgy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T13:28:29-08:00","id":1525477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525369-help-in-making-a-stylized-pack-of-werewolf-foes?p=1525450#post1525450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You said the Tzimisce Knight has some shady deals with Kupala, so they could possibily enlist help by some Banes, this could help but I must ask,why the sorceror is on the path of Thaumaturgy<br /> ?<br /> Just a curious question ,why not Koldunism to make the furrballs combust? ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! He's an odd ball: as they started in Byzantium, he proposed a background as a child and apprentice to Vykos, so I gave him access to regular, Hermetic Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> Currently, Kupala is trying to woo him by offering access to Koldunism!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T06:57:38-08:00","id":1525960,"title":"","content":"Ahhh, that first Transylvanian Chronicles story, tried to run it many times so i remember how thin it is.<br /> <br /> I think the idea of some Kupala aligned spirit infesting the tower is a good one, and a werewolf pack investigating and preparing to battle it might make for an interesting setup and give you an interesting story.<br /> <br /> The werewolves could see an opportunity to have two agents of the Wyrm weaken each other and then mop up the survivors, so be willing to engage in a temporary truce if the coterie helps defeat the demon. The demon could be offering your sorcerer power and help securing the domain it has infested if the coterie will protect it from the werewolves. From the sound of it the composition of your coterie might have some different opinions on this. The setup is a low trust environment with demons, vampires, and cunning werewolves so there isn\u2019t a an obviously good play to go for. The coterie is put into a position where they can engage socially but need to pick a side, and then either betray their temporary allies, or deal with being betrayed. They could also stay out of it, but for the knights that would be pretty cowardly, and whoever wins the fight will know the coterie is going to be setting up havens and be able to return while they\u2019re very vulnerable. Those covered wagons aren\u2019t too hard to light up during the daylight.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: I forget where I saw this, memory from 20+ years ago is a little hazy, but I swear there was something called Kupala's Night where the gauntlet was thin enough that spirits aligned to Kupala could enter the world and traditional Tzimice would battle the spirits (and others could make deals with them). I thought it was in Transylvania by Night but a word search didn't find it, and my other books are real rough scans, but I didn't see it when skimming a few. It feels like it would have been in a Vampire: the Dark Ages book since Dark Ages: Vampire leaned away from Kupala being a real thing and made it more of a myth.<br /> <br /> Anyway, making Kupala's night upcoming could add some pressure, and also setup a way for vampires to engage physically with spirits without dealing with the umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","user":"literatzi","date":". 11-26-2023, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}